<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madhavavarma II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madhavavarma II was the most celebrated king of the Vishnukundina dynasty of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> in the 5th century. His inscriptions credit him with many Vedic sacrifices, including horse sacrifices, which proclaimed his imperial status. He extended Vishnukundina rule over coastal Andhra, while the dynasty also patronised Buddhist monasteries.</p></div>
